  RELEVANCE: Directly addresses the relation between the late Wissenschaftslehre and Fichte's philosophy of history and politics, showing how the turn to the Absolute in the later system is not merely speculative but entails a concrete theory of historical transformation and political legitimacy.

  POSITION: Argues for deep systematic unity between late speculative and political works, grounding Fichte's philosophy of history in the ontology of the Absolute's self-manifestation.
